Q4. Does OCP mean we should never modify
existing code?

Interview Ready Answer

No.

OCP does NOT mean existing code should never
be modified.

It means

New business features should be added by
extending the system instead of modifying
stable existing code.

Existing code can still be modified for

• Bug Fixes.
• Security Updates.
• Performance Improvements.
• Refactoring.
• API Upgrades.

Example

Current System

Payment

↓

UPI Payment

New Requirement

↓

Card Payment

↓

Wallet Payment

↓

Net Banking

Instead of modifying UPI Payment,

Create

CardPayment

WalletPayment

NetBankingPayment

Existing implementation remains unchanged.

